# DISABLED EXAMPLE. Rename to 44-approval-links.caddy inside the gateway's
# /etc/caddy/routes.d/ to serve this group; move it to off/ and `caddy reload`
# to stop serving it.
#
# backend-rs/src/routes/approval_links.rs: NEW routes, written in Rust only
# ("approve or reject a purchase order from a message").
#
#   GET  /api/v1/approval-links/{token}                        public: the page's data (reads only)
#   POST /api/v1/approval-links/{token}/decision               public: the decision, an explicit POST
#   POST /api/v1/inventory/po/{id}/approval/links              analyst+: re-issue and queue the links
#   POST /api/v1/inventory/po/{id}/approval/links/revoke       analyst+: kill every open link
#
# NO PYTHON FAILOVER, on purpose: there is no Python twin of these routes. The
# upstream list names only api-rs; with the Rust container down the gateway
# answers 502 instead of letting Python answer a confusing 404 (FastAPI's own
# "Not Found" is how a stale backend looks, see the running-stockai skill).
# Turning this group off (or never turning it on) is safe ONLY together with
# APPROVAL_LINKS_ENABLED=false on the Python API: with the switch on, an
# approval request puts a link in the message, and a link that nothing answers
# is worse than no link. Turn the switch on AFTER this file is active.
#
# The decision runs through the same function as the in-app approve and reject
# (po_approvals.rs::decide_core), so group 43 may be on or off independently:
# a decision taken in Python (group 43 off) revokes the open links too.
#
# Requires the Python `outbox-drain` worker loop (the links reach people
# through outbound_messages) and a database Python already migrated
# (po_approval_links, po_approvals.decided_channel).
#
# The public page is /aprobar/<token> in the Next.js app; it calls the two
# public routes above through the usual /api rewrite.

@rs_approval_links_public {
	path_regexp ^/api/v1/approval-links/[^/]+(/decision)?$
}
@rs_approval_links_hooks {
	method POST
	path_regexp ^/api/v1/inventory/po/[^/]+/approval/links(/revoke)?$
}
handle @rs_approval_links_public {
	reverse_proxy api-rs:8021 {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
handle @rs_approval_links_hooks {
	reverse_proxy api-rs:8021 {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
